Archiving a message means moving its file under maildir/archive/, and
doing that by hand with notmuch search and mv is slow enough that mail
piles up in the inbox. A tag is quick to set from notmuch-emacs, but it
lives only in the local database: it is lost when the database is
rebuilt and nobody else sees it.

archive turns the tag into the file move. It moves every file of a
message tagged archive that is not already under maildir/archive/
straight into that directory, unchanged and under the same name, and
reindexes so the database follows the move. Running it again moves
nothing. The move is left in the working copy to be committed like any
other change to the list.

maildir/archive/ is a plain directory, not a maildir with its own
cur/, new/ and tmp/. notmuch indexes any file under the database root,
and with maildir.synchronize_flags off no tag depends on which maildir
subdirectory a file sits in, so the extra layout would buy nothing.
---
This is against the mail branch; base-commit is mail@upstream. Like
"[PATCH v2] mail: Add just commit-mail" [1] it appends to the
Justfile, so whichever lands second needs a trivial rebase.

With "[PATCH v2 1/2] notmuch: Tag messages under archive/ as
archived" [2], moved messages get the derived "archived" tag on the
reindex; its path:archive/** rule matches the flat directory as it
did archive/cur/. "[PATCH v2 2/2] zib: Patch review workflow -
Archiving mail" [3] still says files move to maildir/archive/cur/,
so it needs a one-line v3 if this lands.

Tested in a scratch maildir with its own NOTMUCH_CONFIG: tagged
files in cur/ and new/ moved into archive/, untagged ones stayed,
the tag followed the move, path:archive/** matched the moved
messages, and a second run changed nothing.

Changes in v2:
- Move files straight into maildir/archive/ instead of mirroring
  cur/ and new/ under it, as Pat asked. Nothing reads the maildir
  subdirectory, and the recipe drops from 16 lines to 11.
- Drop the check that a file sits in cur/ or new/. The list has no
  other directory a message could be in, and the search already
  skips archive/.
- Link to v1: id:086d59b6e960b0eec659de1a6b0af6c79171243f.1791650786.git.claude@p7x.dev

